e measures of the interior angles of a triangle is ${180}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{40}^{∘}+z+3z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {40}^{∘}+4z & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 4z & ={140}^{∘} \\\\ z & ={35}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b1f86d8-805c-55c7-8e8c-d96d99e3636b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Angles in Triangles With Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56016c12-a1ed-578a-a2c8-65eb76af2295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56016c12-a1ed-578a-a2c8-65eb76af2295" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487737} :answer-field/id #uuid "73cfc52c-c046-5801-a5f6-acb23fafd4cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b302caff-8016-5932-bece-17fa5667969f" :question/math-academy-id "q-235974" :question/problem "![](images/d2/d24c4077069b1de16c64e3179b8e60094e0440ed0a95ac3525297af85899bec2.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $C$ given that $m∠A=m∠B.$\n\n$m∠C=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "Using $m∠A=m∠B,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A & =m∠B \\\\ 8w-{2}^{∘} & =9w-{10}^{∘} \\\\ w & ={8}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, substituting $w={8}^{∘}$ in the expression for $m∠A,$ we get\n\n$$\nm∠A=8({8}^{∘})-{2}^{∘}={62}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find $m∠C$ using the fact that the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2m∠A+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 2\\cdot {62}^{∘}+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {124}^{∘}+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠C & ={56}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073741 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fdb1e0fe-da89-5d80-b9a0-82d4daddc396" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Angle in a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39519a65-41fa-58d3-a9ab-af15c15632f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{29}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487678} {:answer/id #uuid "51d79d3e-ffef-54c3-b160-38d95fa8a3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{33}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487729} {:answer/id #uuid "c6ed0507-243d-5635-bf43-6ed307ba7acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487946} {:answer/id #uuid "cddeecfe-39d9-5a7e-b481-f79efa573fa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{34}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487960} {:answer/id #uuid "de713acd-b8a8-581b-8169-02492745c3da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6ed0507-243d-5635-bf43-6ed307ba7acc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487946} :answer-field/id #uuid "62b01f1f-915d-551f-87fc-c511ebf0a88a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186071276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1769a383-2122-517d-a6f5-ae3c81a6f9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-4181" :question/problem "![](images/72/7210d4af96bf9c4c6c347b9dd91712b14aa9cd8cc21ed5f8535e0546db03068e.png)\n\nDetermine the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles in any triangle is equal to ${180}^{∘}$, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{107}^{∘}+{41}^{∘}+x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {148}^{∘}+x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={32}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488248 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073744 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b1f86d8-805c-55c7-8e8c-d96d99e3636b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Angles in Triangles With Congruent Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a140f24-1574-536e-a402-9186f0265c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{142}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487712} {:answer/id #uuid "7198c182-7e69-556f-8828-1be934a1bff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{140}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487794} {:answer/id #uuid "b98068a7-539d-5a8e-bff3-4725f2627d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{145}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487918} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa8bbd2-1732-5a88-94b6-937ec4e24956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{135}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488007} {:answer/id #uuid "ecca6518-9e4e-54fd-940e-9f0c7f5081ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{137}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7198c182-7e69-556f-8828-1be934a1bff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{140}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487794} :answer-field/id #uuid "428e655b-e554-55ca-bcdc-4ce5b455e62e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a74d4f60-688d-582a-8efa-ef124e45e804" :question/math-academy-id "q-77535" :question/problem "![](images/00/0086a1608c554544cdfc3337e5df136ada8986743ebc2329f262ffc90dbe28e7.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $A$ given that $m∠B=m∠C.$" :question/worked-solution "Using $m∠B=m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠B & =m∠C \\\\ z+{10}^{∘} & =2z \\\\ z & ={10}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, substituting $z={10}^{∘}$ in the expression for $m∠C,$ we get\n\n$$\nm∠C=2({10}^{∘})={20}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find $m∠A$ using the fact that the internal angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+2m∠C & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+2\\cdot {20}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A+{40}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠A & ={140}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a4f969d-aebf-53b5-ad47-1376bb98dc6a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Quantity Given a Description of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1582d363-43e3-557f-b64f-4cb4121664b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{28}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487613} {:answer/id #uuid "426a2765-d590-5cc1-9700-1a5f35a52d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{32}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487699} {:answer/id #uuid "a10dc0b6-a9c0-5cc0-ae3e-5ca8637ff298" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{24}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487866} {:answer/id #uuid "a14d0a99-5e6f-5312-91d4-a0d9671db4c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487867} {:answer/id #uuid "dba84abf-d50e-5e5b-b957-0ffb364f7f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{19}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba84abf-d50e-5e5b-b957-0ffb364f7f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{19}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487982} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0c343ab-d7ef-53e7-9c87-b563a8763928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "627791d7-dc7c-50b5-b4d8-fdfd901f4303" :question/math-academy-id "q-77542" :question/problem "The measure of one angle in a triangle is four times the measure of another angle, and the measure of the third angle is ${85}^{∘}.$ What is the measure of the smallest angle?" :question/worked-solution "Let $x$ be the measure of the first angle. Then the measure of the second angle is $4x.$\n\nThe sum of the measures of the interior angles must be ${180}^{∘}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4x+{85}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x+{85}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={95}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={19}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nHence, the measure of the smallest angle is ${19}^{∘}.$"}]}
